<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burundian Civil War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1993–2005</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Burundian Civil War was fought from 1993 to 2005 between the Tutsi-dominated army and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> rebel groups. It began after the assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melchior-ndadaye">Melchior Ndadaye</a>, Burundi's first democratically elected Hutu president, in October 1993, and an estimated 300,000 people died. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arusha">Arusha</a> Agreement of 2000 and later ceasefires led to a new constitution and elections in 2005.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/burundian-civil-war.jpg" alt="Burundian Civil War" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RTNB (Burundi National Radio and Television) · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:People_fleeing_during_1993_Burundian_genocide.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
